{%- comment -%}
  Archive product page state for main-product (D-23). Snippets can't return values, so this prints words that
  main-product captures:
  - field 'state' (default): "size" when the product has a Size option shown in the Archive button picker (so
    the Size legend holds the size-guide link), then "start" when the page opens in the "Select a size" state.
    That needs: the variant picker's "Start with no size selected" on, more than one size, no ?variant= in the
    URL (product.selected_variant is blank) and something in stock. With a dropdown picker it prints nothing,
    and the size-guide popup keeps its own link.
  - field 'guide': the ID of the popup block marked "Show in the Size legend", if any.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product (required)
  - blocks: {Array} section.blocks of main-product (required)
  - field: {String} 'state' or 'guide'

  Usage:
  {%- capture flags -%}{% render 'pb-product-flags', product: product, blocks: section.blocks %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if field == 'guide'
    for pb_block in blocks
      if pb_block.type == 'popup' and pb_block.settings.pb_size_legend
        echo pb_block.id
        break
      endif
    endfor
  else
    for pb_option in product.options_with_values
      assign pb_option_handle = pb_option.name | handleize
      if pb_option_handle != 'size'
        continue
      endif

      # The Size legend (and its size-guide link) only exists in the Archive button picker.
      assign pb_picker = blocks | where: 'type', 'variant_picker' | first
      if pb_picker.settings.picker_type != 'button'
        break
      endif

      echo 'size '
      if pb_picker.settings.pb_size_start
        if pb_option.values.size > 1 and product.selected_variant == blank and product.available
          echo 'start'
        endif
      endif
      break
    endfor
  endif
-%}
